Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Derive StarkSoundV from single-size soundness and (W)
 (liftExtract)

Circuit/Lift.lean:
- StarkSoundL: single-size soundness at N. Terms vanish at every big row with
  preprocessed columns lifted, and two-sample columns are periodic.
- LiftOK: (W) per component.
- liftExtract, starkSoundV_of_lift, plain_soundL.
- liftOK_of_offsets: (W) for every component whose main columns have at most
  two offsets.

Block/LiftW.lean:
- hashSysW: (W) named per hashSys component.
- (W) proven for bytes, fields, merkle, tables, walk, ctx, wmerkle and undo.
- hashSysW_of_hard: reduces the system to the seven components with
  three-or-more-offset columns.

Existing statements are unchanged. Standard axioms only.

